   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize Scott Hoag to receive certain service credit under section\n384-d of the retirement and social security law",
    "basePrintNo": "S8088",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8088-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8088\n\nSPONSOR: GRIFFO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize Scott Hoag to receive certain service credit under\nsection 384-d of the retirement and social security law\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to allow City of Rome Police Officer Scott\nHoag, who through no fault of his was unable to participate in the twen-\nty-year retirement plan contained in section 384-d of the retirement and\nsocial security law, to participate in that plan and sets forth that all\ncosts shall be paid by the City of Rome.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill allows Scott Hoag to retroactively participate in\nthe special twenty-year retirement plan through the City of Rome as the\napplication was not timely filed through no fault of the officer. This\nsection also elects that the City of Rome will file with the state comp-\ntroller within six months of the effective date a resolution of its\nlocal legislative body together with a certification that the officer\ndid not bar himself from participation in such retirement plan.\n\nSection 2 sets forth that all costs shall be borne by the City of Rome\nand may be amortized over a ten-year period.\n\nSection 3 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThrough no fault of his own, City of Rome Police Officer Scott Hoag was\nunable to timely file an application to participate in the special twen-\nty-year retirement plan contained in section 384-d of the retirement and\nsocial security law. This bill allows Officer Hoag to participate in the\nretirement plan.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2024- S. 9625 - Civil Service and Pensions Committee.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal note in bill.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal note in bill.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n",
